+# Scope and method
+
+Static review on 2026-10-17 of main at
+`a72ca276efbb6c98499878f5c1cdeaadd39c23b8`, after #961 and #962 merged.
+The coordinator inspected core transitions, budgets and shell ownership. Three
+independent domain reviews covered analyzer/target/plan/review,
+process/resource/workspace/metrics, and persistence/configuration/Python tooling.
+Each review traced current writers and readers, failure paths, alternatives and
+existing test assertions, with five distinct self-review passes.
+
+The software-design-philosophy criterion is a reduction in maintained decisions,
+representations or caller obligations. Backward compatibility is not required.
+Current error rejection, historical evidence, platform capabilities and active
+entry points still need their own justification before removal. No runtime test,
+benchmark, build of the implementation or Lean proof was executed in this audit.
+Test-source inspection does not establish a fresh passing test result.
+
+Consulted the catalog overview, architecture, selection, runtime, session/report,
+release provenance and related design records. Prior audits were used to identify
+questions to revisit, not to infer the current result. Source trees outside the
+two recent changes were also inspected, including previously less-covered disk
+statistics and Python release boundaries.
+
+# Assessment
+
+**8.75/10: seven evidenced rows out of eight**, at 1.25 points per row, for the
+inspected boundaries. This is a qualitative assessment, not a repository-wide
+quality measurement or an assertion of complete absence of leakage. The previous
+ranked-request locality finding is resolved; the remaining proposal is a small
+local reduction in maintained statistics.
+
+| Diagnostic | Result | Evidence or missing condition |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Module purposes are describable | Pass | Core transitions, shell execution, discovery, validation and artifact readers have distinct responsibilities. |
+| Interfaces are simpler than implementations | Pass | Typed requests, managed ownership and shared artifact readers hide substantial work. |
+| Implementation rules can change locally | Pass | One normalized Top request now supplies both execution and preview; common source/format rules already have owners. |
+| Interface comments describe abstractions | Pass | Process draining, store transfer and cleanup contracts identify lifetime and evidence limits. |
+| Design discussion occurs in review | Pass | Current maintenance records document alternatives and preservation obligations; this review records rejected changes. |
+| Modules hide important decisions | Pass | Core owns transitions; collectors own retention; workspace/resource modules own cleanup and measurement. The statistics proposal removes local redundancy within that boundary. |
+| Module boundaries are discoverable | Pass | Architecture and knowledge routes describe responsibilities and connect implementation evidence. |
+| 10–20% actual design-time allocation | Unmeasured | No time-allocation measurements were collected, so this row is not awarded. |
+
+No additional module-level failed row was established. An evidenced 10/10 would
+require measuring the investment criterion. Removing the narrow statistics
+redundancy is useful, but does not supply that missing measurement.
+
+# Finding: remove unused and derived disk-monitor state
+
+**Issue: [#963](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/963).** `DiskMonitorStats.latest_owned_bytes` and
+`FilesystemStats.latest` are written for every successful sample but have no
+production reader. Their only external observations are test assertions.
+`DiskMonitorStats.minimum_available_bytes` is separately updated alongside each
+filesystem's historical minimum. Removing the two unused fields and deriving the
+global minimum from the retained per-filesystem minima eliminates three stored
+fields and their update obligations.[^post962-disk-monitor][^post962-shell]
+
+Every accepted reading is nonempty. Under the same mutex, the monitor updates
+all per-filesystem minima and never deletes prior entries. Consequently the
+minimum over all successful readings equals the minimum of the retained
+per-filesystem minima. An empty history yields None; a measured zero remains Some(0). Valid readings
+that trigger a policy stop or arrive after a sticky stop still update statistics. Failed refresh, failed
+measurement and empty capacity maps return before updating statistics. Keep this
+derivation inside the statistics API or snapshot projection, rather than moving
+the aggregation rule into shell.[^post962-disk-monitor]
+
+The local minimum of the current reading remains necessary for immediate stop
+policy. End-of-run free space is a separate explicit measurement in shell and
+must not be replaced with the most recent sampled value. The public report
+field, retained historical minima, sample count, owned-byte peak, maximum duration
+and sticky failure behavior remain unchanged. The proposal makes no performance
+or reproduced-defect claim and adds no enum or generic framework.
+[^post962-disk-monitor][^post962-shell]
+
+Implementation checks should parameterize unmeasured/failed/empty cases and use
+bounded property-generated multi-filesystem sample histories with an independent
+minimum oracle. Include disappearing/reappearing filesystems. Retain existing
+disk-monitor, sticky-stop, final-report and Lean correspondence tests; new formal
+models are unnecessary if only the representation changes. Existing tests that
+read deleted fields should instead verify retained observable statistics.
+
+# Resolved and rejected candidates
+
+| Candidate | Current evidence and decision |
+| --- | --- |
+| Top / TopRange compatibility | #961 removes TopRange. Parser owns omitted-offset normalization and plan consumes the field. Do not reopen #959. [^post962-cli][^post962-plan] |
+| Collector sink/error Options | #962 retains one Result, drops a failed sink and delays error propagation until EOF. Do not reopen #960. [^post962-collector] |
+| Pending output and cleanup classifications | Output continuations are owned by pending completions. Cleanup disposition and report evidence have separate current roles. No restoration of the earlier duplicate maps/classifications was found. [^post962-machine][^post962-shell] |
+| Core flags, diagnostic queue and pending analysis | Attempt history, outcomes and queued diagnostic delivery have distinct consumers. Bundling the one narrow queue/pending producer can rename its invariant but establishes no worthwhile cross-boundary simplification. [^post962-machine] |
+| Run ID and optional session identity | Session identity is set with the report ID on successful load/start and gates persistence. A flag plus shared ID could remove a small copy, but does not remove the session-start condition or repeated policy. No independent Issue justified. [^post962-machine] |
+| Seeded fingerprint constructor | Preflight replaces the initial fingerprint and production uses the ordinary constructor; the seed helper has only a test caller. Removing the tiny helper is possible, but no meaningful current complexity amplification was established. [^post962-machine] |
+| Reservation history | Active reservations, released IDs and allocation frontier serve accounting, repeat-release diagnostics and exhaustion. Inferring released membership from a dense issued prefix is possible, but adds that coupling and reworks corruption/exhaustion contracts for a production path that reserves one aggregate copy grant. No present issue-level benefit established. [^post962-budget] |
+| Disk lifecycle secondary evidence | Incoming primary failure secondaries are moved into the lifecycle history; snapshots project that history into report form. Cleanup can add secondary evidence without a primary stop. This is not two independent mutable copies. [^post962-disk-lifecycle] |
+| Shell task/count/cleanup state | Unaccepted completions differ from JoinSet ownership. Cleanup attempted, safety proven and monitor joined remain distinct after timeout/failure. Final capacity's attempted flag distinguishes unmeasured from failed observation. [^post962-shell] |
+| Resource close result and owned workspace | Blocking close can time out while retaining ownership outside the context. A missing handle is not successful cleanup; replacing the independent result/ownership axes loses evidence. [^post962-shell] |
+| Metrics stage strings | Collector accepts arbitrary stage names, including alpha/zeta in current tests. A fixed enum adds conversions without deleting a policy; shell already centralizes phase mapping. [^post962-metrics][^post962-shell] |
+| Target normalization and analyzer pipelines | Shared lexical/source/candidate conversion rules already exist. Filesystem existence, discovery pruning, pure selection and Vec/spool delivery have distinct contracts. A prepared-selector or generic sink framework adds interfaces without a demonstrated reduction. [^post962-target][^post962-plan][^post962-analyzer] |
+| Analyzer flow/recording state | Working imports, returned continuation evidence, scope restoration and revisit suppression are independent axes. A single enum would combine valid simultaneous states. [^post962-analyzer] |
+| Plan sources, ranking and review evidence | Candidate hashes do not describe files producing zero candidates. Immutable provenance/history differs from current dispatch/applicability; removing these fields discards product evidence. [^post962-plan][^post962-review] |
+| Session and report compatibility | Finalization and completeness are distinct observations. Supported-schema corruption checks and current optional report fields are not obsolete repair paths. Shared structural validation already prevents reader drift. [^post962-session][^post962-report] |
+| Raw configuration and operator cohorts | SessionMode normalizes raw input once. all_legacy supplies a current default/fixture cohort; moving that list elsewhere leaves the same knowledge to maintain. [^post962-config] |
+| Release Result/exception adapters | Typed expected-failure contracts feed current exception-based callers. Removing adapters repeats extraction at callers; deleting Results also removes adopted contracts. No bounded net gain found. [^post962-release] |
+| Provenance and release entry modes | Missing versus verified results already exclude errors. Direct-script/module callers and container capture have live workflow roles. Labels suggesting compatibility do not make those execution environments obsolete. [^post962-provenance][^post962-release-workflow] |
+
+# Review and publication
+
+The coordinator performed the following additional passes; domain reports also
+record five separate reviews of their own findings and rejections.
+
+| Stage | Passes and outcome |
+| --- | --- |
+| Investigation 1 | Pinned main, checked previous PR merges, existing Issues, origin and isolated worktree. |
+| Investigation 2 | Traced core/shell state and budget transitions rather than counting bool/Option fields. |
+| Investigation 3 | Separated current API/error/environment boundaries from obsolete compatibility. |
+| Investigation 4 | Checked timeout, ownership transfer, EOF, unmeasured and failed observation counterexamples. |
+| Investigation 5 | Compared smaller replacements and rejected nominal type changes without meaningful reduction. |
+| Proposal 1 | Repository-wide references confirmed the two latest statistics have no production reader. |
+| Proposal 2 | Checked the global/per-filesystem minimum invariant under the same lock and retained history. |
+| Proposal 3 | Kept current-reading stop policy and separate final capacity observation outside the deletion. |
+| Proposal 4 | Specified independent property expectations and distinguished existing tests from executed evidence. |
+| Proposal 5 | Independent challenge supported the bounded change and added explicit measured-zero and stop-triggering-sample preservation conditions. |
+| Publication 1 | Searched existing Issues for DiskMonitorStats, latest_owned_bytes and minimum_available_bytes; none matched. |
+| Publication 2 | Pinned source links to the audited commit and checked the actual cited update/reader paths. |
+| Publication 3 | Rechecked Japanese Issue scope, low priority, compatibility premise and preserved report behavior. |
+| Publication 4 | Created #963 and read back its OPEN state and exact body, matching the reviewed draft. |
+| Publication 5 | OKF structure, local links, reachability, source IDs/footnotes and all 18 current-source hashes passed across 50 pages. Final site/diff checks are recorded below. |
+
+Final documentation verification on 2026-10-17: OKF structure/local links/
+reachability passed for 50 knowledge pages; changed-page source IDs/footnotes
+and 18 current-source SHA-256 values matched. The strict site build
+(`python -m tools.docs_site --output site`) and `git diff --check` passed.
+These checks validate documentation structure, not runtime behavior.
+
+# Limits and recheck triggers
+
+This audit does not prove runtime correctness, OS behavior, performance, arbitrary
+interleavings or exhaustive absence of compatibility code. Recheck the statistics
+invariant if filesystem history is removed, replaced or reset, if sampling gains
+another writer, or if a new consumer needs latest sampled values. Reevaluate
+other rejected candidates when caller multiplicity, saved schemas, result
+composition or lifecycle ownership changes. Existing passing tests from earlier
+implementation work are not results of this audit.
+
